{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Live instance of this ticket's symptom, observed 2026-09-05 by a working agent (not a probe).\n\nAn agent implementing bug `b2ff-2588-9bb7-4bd2` reported, verbatim:\n\n> One process note: the rebar MCP server returned **502 Bad Gateway** on `set_file_impact` and could not resolve the ticket at all, so tracker ops ran through the local CLI (the documented fallback).\n\nSo the 502 was not confined to a long gate job in this instance — it hit an ordinary short tracker write (`set_file_impact`) and a ticket resolution. The agent fell back to the local CLI and completed its work, which is why nothing downstream broke.\n\n## Host conditions at the time, measured\n\n- local load average **35-44 on 18 cores**, ~40 concurrent pytest processes, two full `make verify` runs (one from another session's worktree);\n- the host's gate admission semaphore **saturated** — `GateCongestedError: all 4 concurrent gate slots in use` was hit independently by three different agents and by one of my own ticket closes;\n- the Gerrit box itself had been restarted at 05:23 UTC (operator-authorised), all containers healthy afterwards.\n\nI am recording the correlation, NOT claiming causation. Two distinct explanations remain open and this observation does not separate them: the 502 may be the MCP container under memory/CPU pressure (this ticket's original framing), or it may be the same host-contention story as `ergophobic-harassed-peacock` (`1e24-bfc0-5f70-4ea4`) and `torrential-unwhite-snail` (`9c2e-b44c-119e-4105`), in which case the three share a root cause and should be reconciled rather than fixed separately.\n\nWhat this DOES add to the ticket: a 502 on a short, cheap tracker call is evidence against the 'only after long gate jobs' framing in the title. Whatever the cause, the trigger is not exclusively long-running work.\n\nAlso worth recording for whoever picks this up: the documented local-CLI fallback WORKED. The agent noticed the 502, switched, and completed — no silent failure and no lost write. That is the system behaving correctly around a degraded component."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788587749528936001,"uuid":"3d13d6e6-7995-4d90-9494-ef6aaf67798c"}